# Phase 06 — Payments

## Goal

Record payments via a single transactional Postgres RPC with validation, audit, receipts, and reversals (append-only).

## Tasks

- One Postgres RPC in a single transaction: insert payment, validate against outstanding balance, write audit log.
- Full and partial payments; methods: cash, UPI, card, bank transfer.
- Idempotency key; derived balance; history and search; receipt screen.
- Reversal flow with confirmation (reversal rows, never deletes).
- Tests: full, partial, overpayment rejected, duplicate submit, reversal, receipt accuracy.

## Done when

- [ ] Payment RPC is transactional and validates balance
- [ ] Full/partial and all methods work; overpayment rejected
- [ ] Idempotency prevents duplicate submits
- [ ] History, search, receipt, and reversal-with-confirm work
- [ ] All listed payment tests pass
- [ ] Lint, typecheck, and tests pass

Update BUILD_STATUS.md, then stop and wait for me.
